=== 1.0.0 (2026-09-04)
* Initial major release of de-dup (re-architected duplicate scanner engine).
* Replaced legacy PyQt5 desktop interface with a lightweight, cross-platform pywebview native desktop shell (macOS WebKit, Windows Edge WebView2, Linux WebKitGTK).
* Implemented native OS file dialog bridge (window.pywebview.api) for native folder browsing and file reveals.
* Added glassmorphic HTML/JS Web Console and Duplicate Results Studio supporting headless servers and remote deployments.
* Integrated lock-free multi-threaded Rust crawler and SIMD hasher engine (dupeguru_rust).
* Re-architected modular Python core pipeline (FileDiscovery, ContentHasher, DuplicateMatcher, TaskRunner, TaskRepository, DBEngine).
* Added cross-database duplicate matching without modifying source databases.
* Standardized pure-Python path resolution across Linux, macOS, and Windows.

=== 4.3.1 (2022-07-08)
* Fix issue where cache db exceptions could prevent files being hashed (#1015)
* Add extra guard for non-zero length files without digests to prevent false duplicates
* Update Italian translations

=== 4.3.0 (2022-07-01)
* Redirect stdout from custom command to the log files (#1008)
* Update translations
* Fix typo in debian control file (#989)
* Add option to profile scans
* Update fs.py to optimize stat() calls
* Fix Error when delete after scan (#988)
* Update directory scanning to use os.scandir() and DirEntry objects
* Improve performance of Directories.get_state()
* Migrate from hscommon.path to pathlib
* Switch file hashing to xxhash with fallback to md5
* Add update check feature to about box

=== 4.2.1 (2022-03-25)
* Default to English on unsupported system language (#976)
* Fix image viewer zoom datatype issue (#978)
* Fix errors from window change event (#937, #980)
* Fix deprecation warning from SQLite
* Enforce minimum Windows version in installer (#983)
* Fix help path for local files
* Drop python 3.6 support
* VS Code project settings added, yaml validation for GitHub actions

=== 4.2.0 (2021-01-24)
